    "turn_text": "He was a Republican nominee. And another one of my favorites was Justice Stevens, who was a Ford nominee. And of course was named by Bush. You know, people forget that Roe v. Wade was written by Harry Blackman, who was a Republican nominee to the court, and a majority, the justices who voted in the majority on Roe v. Wade were Republican nominees. So what we're experiencing in America today is a reflection of the transformation of the Republican Party. which is taking a dramatic hard term to the right and essentially in an effort to marry its corporate status policies with some kind of cultural agenda that would give them some mass popular base, essentially curry favor with the most extreme anti-abortion people in the country and then They were the dog that caught the car and now they're getting their comeuppance as the people of the United States of America beginning in Kansas show them exactly where we are on their pet issue because America is a country where the people still believe in individual freedom and not the Republicans' right-wing, theocratic agenda. conceived by Jerry Falwell Jr. and the other right-wing ministers who want to control the personal medical decisions of the women of America. So, look, on Clarence and Jenny Thomas, I don't know if my view is a little contrarian for the liberals or progressives. She's got a First Amendment right to make an absolute idiot out of herself. And she uses that First Amendment right all the time. You know, just because you're married to someone who is in public office at the Supreme Court or whatever doesn't mean that you surrender your First Amendment rights. So we know exactly where she is. And you know, to some extent, That's better that we know exactly where she is. And of course, where her husband is. They're both basically soldiers in the right wing federalist society movement that is taken over appointments when Republicans are president and taken over the GOP. The problem is in Jenny Thomas. because she can be as maniacal and cultist as she wants to be. It's Clarence Thomas because he's the one who should be governed by ethical restrictions, which don't exist because under the current law that they have given us, the Supreme Court justices decide for themselves whether they have a conflict of interest. They decide for themselves whether they need to recuse a case. So what we're fighting for in Congress is for a real code of ethical responsibility that applies all the way up and down the federal courts, all the way through the Supreme Court. And that's what our focus needs to be on.",
