    "turn_text": "Let me ask you this, I appreciate the passion with which you argue about the importance of the independence of the federal judiciary, the fact that judges are to be impartial arbiters of the law, that we now have a competent United States Attorney General who has been scrupulous in his both public comments and clearly in his leadership of the DOJ, which is now acting like a real DOJ. And I understand the both the brief for the Select Committee to make sure to issue a report that talks about making sure something like this never happens again and that the various right-wing elements that are attacking our democracy are constrained by changes that we make. Yet, the question remains Do you think a criminal referral, which a committee, a select committee can make and in the past select committees have made? Do you think a criminal referral would make a difference positively or negatively?",
